  "figshare_url": "https://data.dtu.dk/articles/dataset/X-ray_fluorescence_XRF_-_Chemical_characterisation_of_brick_clay_and_SSA/30156127",
  "download_disabled": false,
  "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\">Material characterisation: brick clay (yellow and red) and sewage sludge ashes (raw, ED-treated and A2P-treated)</p><p dir=\"ltr\">The chemical composition was determined by semi-quantitative analysis by XRF with a Malvern PanAnalytical Epsilon 4 EDXRF, on fused beads. Fused beads were prepared by mixing 1.6 g of powder sample with 10 g of fluxing agent: 67% lithium tetraborate and 33% lithium metaborate. Oxide content was reported as a percentage of the total sum of measured oxides, including loss on ignition at 1050°C (LoI1050), determined by heating 1 g of the sample for 15 minutes.</p>",
  "funding": "Integration of Underutilized Ashes into Material Cycles by Industry-Urban Symbiosis",
